OL,3,GNEWSAFamily's shock as young sisters
OL,4,Adiagnosed with cancer
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe family of two young sisters who
OL,7,Fwere both diagnosed with cancer say
OL,8,Fthey felt "absolute numbness" at the
OL,9,Fnews and asked medical staff to "double
OL,10,Fcheck" there had not been a mistake.
OL,12,FOdette was three when she was diagnosed
OL,13,Fwith a brain tumour in February 2022
OL,14,Fand has since undergone 15 surgeries.
OL,16,FAfter returning from hospital to her
OL,17,Fhome in Hinckley, Leicestershire, life
OL,18,Ffor the family seemed to be returning
OL,19,Fto a new normal - but in 2024 her
OL,20,Fyounger sister Eliza was diagnosed with
OL,21,Fleukaemia.
OL,23,APub: 10-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,364,360,200,160,0,100
